A||||2||theogre||Why you NEED the check(service) engine light.||||1||
Z||000000||theogre||04-10-2000||07:58 PM||||Today was monday alright......<P>About a mile from work the SES light came on. Stayed on too. Well that sucked. Got into the driveway and checked the code.<P>21 TPS voltage too high<P>special. not.<P>Lunch time clear it and see if it starts. sure enough no start. go to store get new TPS. stuff it in and start right up.<P>Had the SES light not worked I could have been stranded anywhere without a clue as to what the hell was wrong. Instead I had it fixed durring lunch hour.<P>The TPS and crank/coil pickup are about the only sensors the engine will not work without. Missing anything else it runs like a turd but will usually still run.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 04-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||04-10-2000||08:44 PM||||What do you do for a living?  Seems like I read somewhere that you used to be a programmer.  Are you a certified Fiero mechanic now?  I wish I knew 1/2 of what you do.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ozzy||04-10-2000||11:38 PM||||Err...Yeah! I can attest to this. I seem to recall sitting by the side of Interstate 5 with a dead engine... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>Shot crank sensor on DIS '88 Coupe. <P>Ozzy||||reg||14
